<h2>The Complete Guide to Force Urbania Rental and Group Vehicle Hire in Bangalore</h2>
<p>This is the full guide to hiring a Force Urbania in Bangalore and to choosing the right group vehicle when an Urbania is not the right answer. It covers the two Urbania models we operate, how they compare with Tempo Travellers, mini buses and tourist coaches, how to work out the real cost per person, how a quotation is built, what permits and extras mean, and how to plan common group trips. The rates in this guide are the live Yogi Tours &amp; Travels tariff. For the Urbania, that is ₹38 per km, a 300 km daily minimum and ₹700 per day driver Bata, with tolls, parking, permits and state taxes at actuals.</p>

<h2>Part 1. The Force Urbania Explained</h2>

<h3>What is a Force Urbania?</h3>
<p>The Force Urbania is a premium passenger van from Force Motors, the manufacturer behind the long-serving Traveller. Where the Traveller is a rugged workhorse, the Urbania is designed more like a people-mover: a monocoque body, a quiet insulated cabin, a high roof and a ride that feels much closer to a large car. For group travel in India it has become the benchmark for comfort in a van-sized vehicle.</p>
<p>Because of that, "Urbania rental in Bangalore" has become a common search. People want to know where to rent one, how many seats it has, what it costs and whether it is worth the premium over a Tempo Traveller. The sections below answer all of those questions with real numbers.</p>

