<h3>Is there a 21 seater, 15 seater or 10 seater Urbania?</h3>
<p>People search for many Urbania sizes. We operate two: the 17 seater and the 12 seater Maharaja. The Force Urbania platform does not go beyond 17 passengers, so there is no 21 seater Urbania. For 18 to 21 people, the right vehicle is a 21 seater mini bus. If an operator advertises a 21 seater Urbania, ask for the vehicle's registration details and the seating layout before you pay an advance.</p>

<h3>What an Urbania is not</h3>
<p>An Urbania is not always the best value. It costs ₹38 per km against ₹30 for a 17 seater Tempo Traveller and ₹22 for a 12 seater Maharaja Tempo Traveller. For a short trip, a budget-conscious group or a group that will spend most of the day outside the vehicle, a Tempo Traveller is a perfectly good choice. We would rather tell you that than sell you a premium you will not use.</p>

