<h2>Part 10. Glossary</h2>
<table>
<thead><tr><th>Term</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Urbania</td><td>The Force Urbania, a premium passenger van from Force Motors with a monocoque body and a high roof.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Maharaja</td><td>A seating configuration with wide, lounge-style or business-class recliner seats and fewer seats overall.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Tempo Traveller</td><td>A passenger van, commonly the Force Traveller, used widely for group travel in India.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Mini bus</td><td>A smaller bus, usually 21 to 25 seats, between a van and a full coach.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Tourist bus</td><td>A full-size coach, 33 to 50 seats, used for large group tours.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bata</td><td>The daily allowance paid to the driver for food and incidentals on duty.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Daily minimum</td><td>The least number of kilometres billed per day of hire.</td></tr>
<tr><td>AITP</td><td>All India Tourist Permit, which allows tourist vehicles to operate across states, subject to state taxes.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Duty hours</td><td>The standard working window for the driver, 6:00 AM to 10:00 PM.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Billed at actuals</td><td>Charged at the real amount paid, as for tolls, parking and permits.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Captain seat</td><td>An individual seat with its own armrests, as opposed to a shared bench.</td></tr>
</tbody></table>

<h2>Part 11. Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<p><strong>What is the difference between an Urbania and a Tempo Traveller?</strong> The Urbania has a monocoque body, a quieter cabin, a higher roof and a ride closer to a car's. The Tempo Traveller uses the older Traveller van body and is the lower-cost option.</p>
<p><strong>Which is better for a long trip?</strong> For trips over five hours, most groups find the Urbania more comfortable. For shorter trips or tighter budgets, a Tempo Traveller is fine.</p>
<p><strong>Do you offer a 21 seater Urbania?</strong> No. The Urbania seats up to 17. Use the 21 seater mini bus for 18 to 21 people.</p>
<p><strong>What if my group is 13 to 17?</strong> Choose the 17 seater Urbania or the 17 seater Tempo Traveller.</p>
<p><strong>What if my group is 10 to 12?</strong> Choose the 12 seater Maharaja Urbania or the Maharaja Tempo Traveller.</p>
<p><strong>Can I see photos of the Urbania I will get?</strong> Yes. Each Urbania page shows photos of our vehicles, and you can ask for more on WhatsApp.</p>
<p><strong>How do I pay?</strong> Payment terms are in the written quotation. Ask when you enquire.</p>
<p><strong>Can the Urbania go to Goa?</strong> Yes. Interstate permits and state taxes are itemised in the quotation.</p>
<p><strong>Is the Urbania suitable for hill roads?</strong> Yes. It is regularly booked for Coorg, Ooty, Wayanad and Chikmagalur.</p>
<p><strong>Can I get a GST invoice?</strong> Yes, on request.</p>
<p><strong>What if my plan changes?</strong> Tell us as early as possible. See the <a href="/cancellation-policy">cancellation policy</a>.</p>
<p><strong>How early should I book?</strong> For weekends and festival dates, as early as you can. For weekdays, a few days is often enough, and we will tell you what is available.</p>

